{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1311628-lich-using-arete-or-foundation","id":1311628,"title":"Lich using Arete or Foundation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-05-12T16:26:29-07:00","id":1311628,"title":"Lich using Arete or Foundation?","content":"I need some opinions to discuss so that I can reach a conclusion on a matter of relevance in one of my chronicles. So, the thing is in my game there's a Lich who made the rite of transformation in the mythical ages, so he used the Dark Ages mage system for magic, he used Foundation and Pillars in his time etc. Later, after the Tradition Convention of 1466, it's when mages start using Arete and Spheres. So if the said Lich was to be active after the tradition convention and assuming now every other common mage uses Arete and Spheres, would the said Lich still use the Foundation and Pillars from the time of his transformation? What do you think?<br /> <br /> Here we have two arguments, one is that the nature of magic itself changed, so that Arete and spheres would replace Foundation and Pillars after a certain time (let's say 1466 for the said Convention, for simplification's sake). But the other argument is that once you become a Lich you can't change your vision of magic, your enlightment (Arete or Foundation in the alternate system) is frozen in time. What would you do in this situation as a storyteller?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T16:56:38-07:00","id":1311639,"title":"","content":"The standard Mage book answer sides with &quot;the nature of magic itself changed,&quot; as there were extremely old mages around that would have used the Foundation/Pillar system, but use the Arete/Sphere system in modern times (though DA Mage came after most of the standard Mage books).<br /> <br /> VtM contradicts this, as V20 has Foundation/Pillar based mages in it explicit holdovers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T17:12:05-07:00","id":1311643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1311628-lich-using-arete-or-foundation?p=1311639#post1311639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The standard Mage book answer sides with &quot;the nature of magic itself changed,&quot; as there were extremely old mages around that would have used the Foundation/Pillar system, but use the Arete/Sphere system in modern times (though DA Mage came after most of the standard Mage books).<br /> <br /> VtM contradicts this, as V20 has Foundation/Pillar based mages in it explicit holdovers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I know that in The Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra they state the mages from the sect use Foundation/Pillar for their archaic and strange magic, but would you think this should be the case even for the standard hermetic who became a Lich in the mythical age and awoke later when everybody else was using Arete and Spheres?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T17:52:33-07:00","id":1311658,"title":"","content":"What serves the story better?<br /> <br /> I mean, to me, the Lichdom itself is already a bit sticking point that's a huge social problem in mage society. That's going to matter more than which mechanics they use for magic. If I want the Lich to manage to 'fit in' more easily, going Arete/Spheres makes more sense. If I want to make them being accepted by anyone difficult, keeping them at Foundation/Pillars is just one more way to isolate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T18:55:51-07:00","id":1311676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1311628-lich-using-arete-or-foundation?p=1311658#post1311658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What serves the story better?<br /> <br /> I mean, to me, the Lichdom itself is already a bit sticking point that's a huge social problem in mage society. That's going to matter more than which mechanics they use for magic. If I want the Lich to manage to 'fit in' more easily, going Arete/Spheres makes more sense. If I want to make them being accepted by anyone difficult, keeping them at Foundation/Pillars is just one more way to isolate them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In this particular case I'm more interested in the system approach feedback, so to speak. The effects it would have in a chronicle and so on as the story aspect I have already covered in the story, but nobody has seem the being using magic first hand, they only heard stories, so I'm thinking about which route (no pun intended) I would follow as an encounter seems to be approaching. In any case, thanks for the feedback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T23:38:39-07:00","id":1311717,"title":"","content":"Personally I like the stagnation of keeping them on Foundations and Pillars, they are undead but also archaic.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Itarajana keep Pillars because they stay in the underworld and the change of magic hasn't affected them.. (Maybe it's a sub-realm of the underworld created by them in the first place...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T03:00:43-07:00","id":1311739,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting idea, though one that creates its own kind of problems. I'm still unsure which way to follow, but I still have time until the next game session of this particular chronicle. I'm found of the idea of using Foundation/Pillars, also because I really loved the Dark Ages Mage book. The Foundation/Pillars reinforces the idea of different paradigms for magic etc. In any case thanks for the feedback, hopefully I'm gonna get more feedback and an interesting discussion here and irl, so that I take my final decision after thinking well about all the possible issues and consequences of the decision itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T07:03:36-07:00","id":1311774,"title":"","content":"Does everybody agree that a Lich should use Foundation and Pillars instead of Arete?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T12:05:15-07:00","id":1311832,"title":"","content":"No?<br /> <br /> I mean, I hate the Foundation/Pillars scheme (and very specifically the Pillars part). So I'm never going to agree a Lich should use them in general. But I'm willing to acknowledge people like that system and it can be appropriate for some situations to use it like you're talking about doing if that's how you want to go.<br /> <br /> If the Lich is a NPC... it's not like the players - or more importantly the player characters - are going to be able to tell the difference between Foundation/Pillar magic and Arete/Sphere magic. It's just going to be Hermetic magic to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T17:02:12-07:00","id":1311906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1311628-lich-using-arete-or-foundation?p=1311774#post1311774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does everybody agree that a Lich should use Foundation and Pillars instead of Arete?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had an interesting suggestion last night at my gaming group<br /> - Change the Lich on to Arete and Spheres, but make the Paradigm for the Lich match the old Foundation. So- The poor Lich is using the right magic system, but is limited to magic that could have been cast in the past under the foundation system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T17:20:37-07:00","id":1311907,"title":"","content":"But... there's no difference...<br /> <br /> A Hermetic from DA and a Hermetic from, say, the Sorcerer's Crusade era can cast all the same things assuming they have the appropriate (if different) stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T17:58:24-07:00","id":1311918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1311628-lich-using-arete-or-foundation?p=1311907#post1311907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... there's no difference...<br /> A Hermetic from DA and a Hermetic from, say, the Sorcerer's Crusade era can cast all the same things assuming they have the appropriate (if different) stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, they could cast the same things, but the magic follows the change of codification of the spheres and Arete.<br /> That's actually the aim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}